{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":19,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.chainCarrier_joins_consecutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.chainCarrier_joins_consecutive","kind":"theorem","line":230,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.lean#L230-L234","doc":"…and the joins really are inhabited where they should be, so\n`splitsOff_or_consecutive` is cutting something out rather than describing an empty\nrelation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.consecutive_has_no_separable_component","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.consecutive_has_no_separable_component","kind":"theorem","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.lean#L217-L228","doc":"**The trichotomy is sharp.** On the chain carrier no component of the consecutive\ntriple `{i, i+1, i+2}` splits off, so those 31 triples are genuinely outside this\nfile's reach rather than merely left unproved by it. Without this the disjunction above\ncould be read as an artifact of a weak `PathCarrier`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.chainCarrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.chainCarrier","kind":"def","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.lean#L207-L215","doc":"The chain carrier: consecutive components joined and linked, everything else free.\nInstantiated so the statements above are demonstrably about a real configuration. The\nvalue `-2` is what the probe measures in the all-`σ⁻¹` branch; nothing depends on it\nbeyond being nonzero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.splitsOff_or_consecutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.splitsOff_or_consecutive","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.lean#L183-L205","doc":"**The residual is exactly the consecutive triple.** On the path carrier an ordered\ntriple either has a component that splits off — putting it inside\n`splitsOff_of_unlinked`'s reach — or it is `{a, a+1, a+2}`. There is no third case.\n\nSo the 31 triples the carrier leaves uncovered are not a ragged remainder to be chipped\nat with more linking-number bookkeeping; they are one shape, and closing them needs a\ngenuinely different invariant (see the header). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.not_adjacent_of_lt_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.not_adjacent_of_lt_lt","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.lean#L176-L181","doc":"The two outer members of an ordered triple are never adjacent — `a < b < c` forces\n`c ≥ a + 2`. Small, but it is what makes the trichotomy below a trichotomy: the pair\n`(a, c)` is unlinked in every case, so only `(a,b)` and `(b,c)` can vary. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.PathCarrier.lk_zero_of_not_adjacent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.PathCarrier.lk_zero_of_not_adjacent","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.lean#L174-L174","doc":"non-consecutive components are unlinked ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.PathCarrier.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.PathCarrier.mk","kind":"ctor","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.lean#L172-L172","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.PathCarrier.toSummands","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.PathCarrier.toSummands","kind":"def","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.lean#L172-L174","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.PathCarrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.PathCarrier","kind":"structure","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.lean#L160-L174","doc":"The path carrier: `lk` vanishes off consecutive pairs. Stated in the direction\nactually used — non-adjacent implies unlinked — so nothing below silently requires more\nthan the measurement supports.\n\n**This hypothesis is no longer a measurement (2026-09-05).**\n`MonotoneWordComponentStructure.linking_only_between_adjacent` proves it for every\nmonotone word: a run crossing two distinct components puts them at `compIdx g` and\n`compIdx g + 1`, so only consecutive components can be linked. The `P_μ` shape was\ncarried as a measured fact across this whole arc — 7 isotopes, both crossing-resolution\nbranches — and it is a theorem. Kept as a structure field because the consumers below\ntake a carrier as given; it is now an *instantiable* hypothesis rather than an assumed\none. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.instDecidableAdjacent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.instDecidableAdjacent","kind":"instance","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.lean#L157-L158","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.Adjacent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.Adjacent","kind":"def","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.lean#L153-L155","doc":"Adjacency on the path `P_μ` that the derived carrier's linking graph is measured to\nbe: `lk ≠ 0` exactly on consecutive components. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.allSplitOff_of_delta_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.allSplitOff_of_delta_zero","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.lean#L134-L151","doc":"The merged `Δ = 0` result, recovered: when *all three* pairwise linking numbers\nvanish, *every* component splits off from the other two — three applications of\n`splitsOff_of_unlinked`, none of which needs the third hypothesis. Kept so the\nstrengthening is visibly a strengthening rather than a different claim.\n\nSymmetry of `lk` is taken as an explicit hypothesis rather than added to `Summands`:\nthe merged sibling's `Δ = 0` theorem pairs its three hypotheses with its three\nconclusions in matching index order and so never needs it, whereas `SplitsOff k i j`\nfixes `k` first and does. Linking numbers are symmetric — the sibling\n`FreedmanHeGenusHandleNeedsVanishingLinking.lean` carries `lk_symm` as a field — so\nthis asks for nothing the topology does not give; it is stated so the dependence is\nvisible instead of assumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.splitsOff_of_unlinked","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.splitsOff_of_unlinked","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.lean#L124-L132","doc":"**The result, and it is the whole file.** One component unlinked from the other two\nis enough — the pair may be linked to each other arbitrarily.\n\nThis is the contrapositive of `joins_linked` applied twice, which is why it is as\ngeneral as the connected-sum decomposition itself. The merged `Δ = 0` theorem asks for\nall three pairwise linking numbers to vanish; only these two are used. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.SplitsOff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.SplitsOff","kind":"def","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.lean#L118-L122","doc":"Component `k` **splits off** from the pair `i, j` when it shares a summand with\nneither. This is what makes `μ̄` vanish on `{i, j, k}`: `λ_k` is then trivial in the\nquotient generated by the meridians of `i` and `j`, so the `h_i h_j` coefficient is\nzero. Note it says **nothing** about whether `i` and `j` are linked to each other. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.Summands.joins_linked","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.Summands.joins_linked","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.lean#L116-L116","doc":"sharing a summand makes two components linked ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.Summands.lk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.Summands.lk","kind":"def","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.lean#L114-L114","doc":"linking numbers of the closure ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.Summands.joins","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.Summands.joins","kind":"def","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.lean#L112-L112","doc":"some summand of the connected sum touches both components ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.Summands.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.Summands.mk","kind":"ctor","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.lean#L110-L110","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.Summands","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.Summands","kind":"structure","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/OneSeparatedComponentSufficesForMilnorVanishing.lean#L105-L116","doc":"Two components are **joined** when some summand of the connected-sum\ndecomposition touches both. On a monotone closure a summand is one generator's run, so\nit touches only the components containing strands `g` and `g+1` — measured at most two.\nThe single hypothesis `joins_linked` is what the topology supplies: a shared\n`(2, k)` torus summand links the two components it joins. ","signatureChunk":0}]}